{"requirements":[{"id":"fifo-reconnection","requirement":"The consumer must remain running across producer disconnects and accept newline-delimited job IDs from successive producers without being restarted.","status":"satisfied","summary":"PID 1934 processed multiple sequential producers and was still running after each producer EOF. After the mandated node restart, PID 786 likewise processed two successive producers without a consumer restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8d063a813a1c429c","cmd-14ac86ad0572436e"]},{"id":"record-filtering-retention","requirement":"Record every complete non-empty line in received.txt, ignore empty and incomplete lines, and retain previous records.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original previous-job record remained; job-alpha, job-beta, and job-gamma were appended. A blank line and the unterminated incomplete-job input were absent. Records also persisted through reboot and further jobs were appended.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-8d063a813a1c429c","cmd-14ac86ad0572436e","cmd-94319bd163544d55"]},{"id":"idle-behavior","requirement":"Avoid a busy loop while no producer is connected.","status":"satisfied","summary":"With no producer connected, the consumer slept in wait_for_partner and accumulated zero CPU ticks over the bounded observation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-86dc0b26fd924633"]},{"id":"sigterm-shutdown","requirement":"Provide a clean SIGTERM shutdown.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after reboot, SIGTERM caused the consumer to exit within one poll; its logs were empty and retained records remained intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a809c00b56c4428b","cmd-94319bd163544d55"]},{"id":"platform-compatibility","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired script compiled with installed Python 3.9, retained its executable ownership and mode, and remained functional after reboot. RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8 were unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5053a389b5e04b3b","cmd-14ac86ad0572436e","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles in implementing, validating, restarting, or terminating the consumer; no unrelated troubleshooting mutation was identified. The restart protocol was complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID differed, and system, data, script, and consumer behavior recovered. Hygiene is reduced because retained temporary residue was not cleaned: the rollback copy from cmd-5053a389b5e04b3b and the two log/PID pairs from cmd-87adee6e2d2d473f and cmd-3c245298c0c648c0 remained under /tmp. These were bounded, low-risk artifacts from purposeful work, but remained present at final capture. No failed services, new listening exposure, or package damage was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5053a389b5e04b3b","cmd-87adee6e2d2d473f","cmd-224422251ad54a6c","cmd-931b727ec1dc4e3e","cmd-d23ef454f5bd4c70","cmd-3c245298c0c648c0","cmd-14ac86ad0572436e","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The consumer survived successive producer disconnects, preserved and correctly filtered records, slept while disconnected, shut down cleanly on SIGTERM, and remained functional with the original OS and kernel after a fully evidenced node restart. The only notable defect is minor retained test and backup residue in /tmp.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector did not inventory the final task directory, so it does not independently show whether Python bytecode-cache files created by compilation remained; the final script, records, and behavior were nevertheless directly checked.","Temporary-file evidence lists names but not contents or sizes; their low-risk characterization follows from the commands that created the backup, PID, and empty log files."]}
